cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Smart Research Web Scraper
message: >-
  If you use this software to collect data for a publication, please cite it and
  attach the provenance manifest and extraction recipe that the run produced.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Merwan
    family-names: Roudane
    email: merwanroudane920@gmail.com
    orcid: null
repository-code: https://github.com/merwanroudane/webscrap
url: https://webscrapapp.streamlit.app/
abstract: >-
  A research-oriented web data acquisition tool for people who do not program.
  It profiles a source, prefers deterministic extraction over language models,
  refuses private and metadata network addresses, respects robots.txt, and emits
  a provenance manifest, a data dictionary and a re-runnable extraction recipe
  alongside every dataset, so that a published result can be reproduced.
keywords:
  - web scraping
  - research data
  - reproducibility
  - provenance
  - data collection
  - streamlit
license: MIT
